API functions
Create frontend/src/api.js with:
const API_BASE_URL =
  import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE_URL || "http://localhost:8000/api";

export const createEntry = (payload) =>
  axios.post(`${API_BASE_URL}/entries`, payload);

export const getEntries = () =>
  axios.get(`${API_BASE_URL}/entries`);

export const getEntry = (id) =>
  axios.get(`${API_BASE_URL}/entries/${id}`);

export const verifyChain = () =>
  axios.get(`${API_BASE_URL}/verify`);

export const exportLog = () =>
  axios.get(`${API_BASE_URL}/export`);

export const healthCheck = () =>
  axios.get(`${API_BASE_URL}/health`);
Create-entry request
The form should send:
{
  "data": "Payment received",
  "user_id": "Alice",
  "file_hash": null,
  "metadata": {}
}
Only data is required.
Entry response
The frontend should expect:
{
  "id": 1,
  "user_id": "Alice",
  "data": "Payment received",
  "file_hash": null,
  "timestamp": 1710000000000,
  "prev_hash": "GENESIS",
  "entry_hash": "abc123...",
  "nonce": 0,
  "metadata": {},
  "created_at": "2026-08-22 12:00:00"
}
Verification response
For a valid chain:
{
  "valid": true,
  "tampered_at": null,
  "total_entries": 3,
  "message": "Chain is valid"
}
For a tampered chain:
{
  "valid": false,
  "tampered_at": 2,
  "total_entries": 3,
  "message": "Tampering detected at entry #2"
}
For now, your friend can use mock data matching these response formats. When the backend endpoints are ready, they only need to replace the mock functions with the real API calls.
Tell your friend not to edit anything inside backend/. The frontend work should stay inside frontend/.